Setup for code-generation format

Block_Matrix = n x m blocks 
- block_row_sizes[n], block_column_sizes[m]
- column_indices[n*m*sum(block_column_sizes)]	 <- pointer into sparse data vector
- column_nnz[n*m*sum(block_column_sizes)] 		 <- nnz in each column
- block_index[n,m] 								 <- index into column_indices to the first column of the block

Operations:
- initialize
- copy a dense block in
- copy a sparse block in
- compute jacobian
-- function call order 



What is actually called at the end of the day?

---- Evaluation ----

out.segment<size>(ind) = dynamics_eq::eval(param, x.template segment<size>(ind), x.segment(ind, size)...);
out.segment(ind,size) = dynamics_eq::eval(param, x.segment(ind, size), x.segment(ind, size)...);
for(int i=0; i< ...)
	out.segment(ind,size) = dynamics_eq::eval(param, x.segment(ind, size), x.segment(ind, size)...);
out.segment(ind,size) = dynamics_eq::eval(param, x.segment(ind, size), x.segment(ind, size)...);
out.segment<size>(ind) = dynamics_eq::eval(param, x.segment(ind, size), x.segment(ind, size)...);


---- Jacobian ----

out.segment<size>(ind) 
	= dynamics_eq::jac(param, x.segment<size>(offset), x.segment<size>(offset), ..., jac_offsets<num_inputs>(offset)),

out.SEG(ind,size) 
	= dynamics_eq::jac(param, x.SEG(offset,size), x.SEG(offset,size), ..., jac_offsets<num_inputs>(offset), jac_ptr),



/**
 * jac_offsets: vector of length num_inputs with offsets to write the columns into jac_ptr
 */
function jac(param, x1,x2,x3, jac_offsets, jac_ptr)
